---
import TimerPage from '@/layouts/TimerPage.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import { faqs } from '@/data/faqs';
import { relatedTimers, relatedPosts } from '@/data/related';
import { defaultConfigs } from '@/engine/presets';
import { beeps } from '@/data/beeps';
import { workouts } from '@/data/workouts';
---

<TimerPage
  title="Interval Timer – Free Work, Rest and Rounds Timer"
  description="Free online interval timer for HIIT, circuits and repeating reminders. Set work, rest and rounds, and you'll hear a beep at every change. Works offline."
  path="/interval"
  h1="Interval timer"
  lede="This interval timer switches between work and rest for as many rounds as you like. It beeps at every change, so you can put your phone down and move."
  config={defaultConfigs.interval}
  faq={faqs['/interval']}
  related={relatedTimers['/interval']!}
  posts={relatedPosts['/interval']}
  crumbName="Interval timer"
>
  <Section title="Set it up" flush>
    <p>
      Work is the hard part and Rest is the easy part. Rounds is how many times you repeat the pair.
      On this page, Work and Rest are in minutes. Type a number or tap − and +. Start takes you
      straight into the first work block. The rest after the last round is included, so you finish
      on a breather, not a sprint.
    </p>
    <p>
      The default is 30 minutes of work and 5 minutes of rest, eight times. For a simple repeating
      reminder, set Rest to 0 and it just beeps every few minutes. With 30 minute blocks and eight
      rounds, you get a beep every half hour for four hours.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section title="Run it">
    <p>
      Press Start or the Space key. Work shows a pulse icon and Rest shows a wind icon. The sounds
      differ too. A rising pair means go and a falling pair means ease off. You'll hear a tick in
      the last three seconds and three notes at the finish. Pause holds the clock right where it is.
    </p>
    <p>
      Esc or End session always asks before stopping. While the timer runs, it keeps your screen
      awake where the browser allows it, so your phone won't go dark in round six. On a computer,
      the tab title counts down too, so you can check it from another tab.
    </p>
  </Section>
  <Section title="Ready-made">
    <p>
      Want a head start? These pages open with the timer already set for a named workout or a
      repeating beep.
    </p>
    <ul class="links">
      {workouts.map((w) => (
        <li>
          <a href={w.path}>{w.h1}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
      {beeps.map((b) => (
        <li>
          <a href={b.path}>{b.h1}</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </Section>
</TimerPage>
